    Upon reflection of recent discussions, I've changed my stance somewhat. While initial thoughts focused primarily on immediate concerns such as violent acts and social misbehavior (Certainly probably dislike) Initially, i did not believe ECONOMICS WAS THE MOST IMPORTANT PROBLEM FACING AMERICA TODAY.

With fresh insights garnered during online exchanges however,I’m persuaded by compelling arguments weighing economics’ pivotal position — notably considering its potential impact on far-reaching effects stemming from financial insecurity.



   Consequently, leaning closer to acceptance;
